   "text": {
    "L1": "Grandma Imna tells an old tale about people and tigers arguing about who was stronger.",
    "L2": "The tale becomes Hekko, a game with two sides: Aami and Aakho.",
    "L3": "The Aami stand inside a big circle and hold hands tightly.",
    "L4": "The Aakho try to push the Aami out. Holding together makes the Aami hard to push.",
    "L5": "When a tiger is caught, the tiger says, Joko, which means I give up.",
    "L6": "Here is a useful rule: The Aami must hold hands inside the circle.",
    "L7": "A common mistake is to say, The Aami must to hold hands.",
    "L8": "After must, use the plain action word: hold, not to hold.",
    "L9": "Now you can describe another traditional game in a few clear sentences."
   },
